ification for the SQ-5 setup (Patching, Preamp, HPF, Gate, 4-band PEQ, Compressor, Aux 1–4 Pre-Fader sends, Aux 1–4 Master EQ & Safety Limiter, FX1 Reverb, Layer A layout).\n     - Located the installed SQ-MixPad application at `C:\\Program Files\\Allen & Heath\\SQ MixPad 1.6.1\\SQ MixPad.exe` and its help documentation at `C:\\Program Files\\Allen & Heath\\SQ MixPad 1.6.1\\help\\Connection_Help.html`.\n     - Extracted and decompressed the official embedded **SQ-5 default template (`SQ5.DAT`)** from `SQ MixPad.exe`'s Qt resource table (`Raw offset 2837251`, compressed length `0x09BB = 2491`, uncompressed length `0x20000 = 131,072` bytes) and saved it to:\n       `C:\\Users\\brazi\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\7c40d475-4f8e-4ff9-9d8a-99008f2e1cda\\SQ5.DAT`.\n     - Reverse-engineered `cShowManager`, `cScene`, `cScene::CalcSceneCRC`, `SerialiseScene`, `SerialiseChannel`, and `Recipient` classes in `SQ MixPad.exe` and verified the exact CRC-32 checksum algorithm (`0xD0FD198F` on `SQ5.DAT` matches 100%).\n   - **In Progress**:\n     - Finalizing the exact parameter values in `NVDATA.DAT` (based on `SQ5.DAT`), recalculating the CRC-32 at `0x1FFFC`, and writing `SHOW.DAT` + `NVDATA.DAT` to the `AHSQ/SHOWS/SHOW0000` directory and `CurrentShow`.\n\n3. **Key Findings (Exact Binary Specification of SQ-5 Showfiles V1.6)**\n   - **PE Sections of `SQ MixPad.exe`**:\n     - `.text`: `RVA = 0x001000`, `Raw = 0x000400` (`RVA = Raw + 0x0C00`)\n     - `.rdata`: `RVA = 0x26A000`, `Raw = 0x268600` (`RVA = Raw + 0x1A00`)\n   - **Directory Structure (`AHSQ`)**:\n     - Root folder: `AHSQ` containing `SHOWS`, `SCENES`, `LIBRARY`.\n     - Show subfolder inside `AHSQ/SHOWS`: `SHOW0000` (must match regex `SHOW\\d{4}`).\n     - Inside `SHOW0000`:\n       1. `SHOW.DAT`: **17 bytes** (`0x11` bytes). Bytes `0..15` are the ASCII show name (e.g., `\"3Voix 4Casques\\0\\0\"`), padded with `0x00`, and byte `16` (`0x10`) is `0x00`.\n       2. `NVDATA.DAT`: **131,072 bytes** (`0x20000` bytes). Exact same binary format as `SQ5.DAT`.\n   - **CRC-32 Algorithm (`cScene::CalcSceneCRC` at `Raw 0x0E0950`)**:\n     - Uses standard IEEE 802.3 256-entry lookup table located in `SQ MixPad.exe` at `Raw = 0x28F120 - 0x1A00 = 0x28D720`.\n     - Computes CRC over `NVDATA.DAT` bytes `0x00014` (`20`) through `0x1FFFB` (`131067`) inclusive:\n       ```csharp\n       uint crc = 0;\n       for (int i = 0x14; i < 0x1FFFC; i++) {\n           crc = ~crc;\n           uint idx = (crc ^ buf[i]) & 0xFF;\n           crc = (crc >> 8) ^ table[idx];\n           crc = ~crc;\n       }\n       // Write BitConverter.GetBytes(crc) to buf[0x1FFFC .. 0x1FFFF]\n       ```\n   - **`NVDATA.DAT` (`SQ5.DAT`) Layout & Sentinels**:\n     - `0x00038`: Sentinel 1 (`01 A5 A5 A5`) — Surface Layers (`Layer A`..`Layer F` at `0x0068`, each `97` (`0x61`) bytes: 1 flag byte `0xFF` + 32 strips of 3 bytes `[Type, Index, 0x00]`).\n       - Strip `Type = 0x01` (Audio channel), `Index`:\n         - `0x00..0x02` (`0..2`) = `Ip 1`, `Ip 2`, `Ip 3` (`Voix 1..3`)\n         - `0x40` (`64`) = `FX1 Ret`\n         - `0x58..0x5B` (`88..91`) = `Aux 1` .. `Aux 4` (`Casque 1..4`)\n         - `0x68` (`104`) = `Main LR`\n         - `0x6B` (`107`) = `FX1 Send`\n         - Unassigned / Blank strip = `00 00 00`.\n     - `0x00370`: Sentinel 2 (`02 A5 A5 A5`) — **122 Channels** starting at `0x00374`, each **`0x150` (`336`) bytes** (`channelOffset = 0x0374 + chIndex * 0x150`).\n       - Inside each `0x150`-byte channel record (`base = 0x0374 + ch * 0x150`):\n         - **`+0x000 .. +0x005` (6 bytes)**: **Channel Name** (max 6 ASCII chars, null-padded, e.g., `\"Voix 1\"`, `\"Voix 2\"`, `\"Voix 3\"`, `\"Casq 1\"`, `\"Casq 2\"`, `\"Casq 3\"`, `\"Casq 4\"`, `\"Reverb\"`).\n         - **`+0x006` (1 byte)**: `0x00` (null terminator).\n         - **`+0x00C` (1 byte)**: **Channel Color** (`0` = Off, `1` = Red, `2` = Yellow, `3` = Green, `4` = Cyan, `5` = Blue, `6` = Purple, `7` = White).\n         - **`+0x034` (`uint16` LE)**: Preamp Gain (default `0x0064` = `100` = +28dB; each step is `0.00390625` or `1/256` or index `0..100` where `0x3A` is pad/48V).\n         - **`+0x054 .. +0x05B` (HPF)**:\n           - `+0x054` (`uint16` LE): HPF Frequency (`0x5396` default = ~100 Hz; log scale `0x0000..0xFFFF` over `20 Hz..20 kHz`: `freq_u16 = round(log(Hz / 20.0) / log(1000.0) * 65535)` — verify: `20 * 1000^(0x4797/65535) = 20 * 1000^(18327/65535) = 138 Hz`, wait: for PEQ `20..20000 Hz`, `0x4797 = 18327`, `0x6811 = 26641`, `0xA72E = 42798`, `0xCB30 = 52016` -> `20 * (1000)^(x/65535)` gives `138 Hz`, `330 Hz`, `1825 Hz`, `4800 Hz`, or `16 * (1250)^(x/65535)`: let's check `PEQ` freq formula in `UnitsHelper` at `0x059DC0`!).\n           - `+0x057` (`uint8`): **HPF In/Out** (`0x00` = OFF, `0x01` = ON; note `+0x056` is `0x01` in default `SQ5.DAT`).\n         - **`+0x05C .. +0x079` (Gate)**:\n           - `+0x05C` (`uint16` LE): Attack (`0x32A6` default)\n           - `+0x05E` (`uint16` LE): Hold (`0x7B60` default)\n           - `+0x060` (`uint16` LE): Release (`0x7878` default)\n           - `+0x062` (`uint16` LE): Threshold (`0x6200` default = `-30 dB` in `32768 + dB*256`: `32768 - 30*256 = 25088 = 0x6200`! Exact match! So `-42 dB` = `32768 - 42*256 = 22016 = 0x5600`!)\n           - `+0x064` (`uint16` LE): Depth (`0x9400` default = `20 dB`: `32768 + 20*256 = 37888 = 0x9400`! Exact match! So `12 dB` = `32768 + 12*256 = 35840 = 0x8C00`!)\n           - `+0x076` (`uint8`, `sNVData + 0x916` -> `+0x05C + 0x1A = +0x076`): **Gate In/Out** (`0x00` = OFF, `0x01` = ON).\n         - **`+0x07C .. +0x0AD` (4-Band PEQ)**:\n           - 4 bands at `+0x07C` (LF), `+0x082` (LM), `+0x088` (HM), `+0x08E` (HF), each 6 bytes:\n             - `+0..1` (`uint16` LE): **Gain** (`32768 + round(dB * 256)`, so `0 dB` = `0x8000`, `-3.0 dB` = `0x7D00`, `-2.5 dB` = `0x7D80`, `+1.5 dB` = `0x8180`, `+2.0 dB` = `0x8200`, `-1.5 dB` = `0x7E80`).\n             - `+2..3` (`uint16` LE): **Frequency** (default LF=`0x4797`, LM=`0x6811`, HM=`0xA72E`, HF=`0xCB30